# SEO Analyzer Platform Blueprint (SEMrush/Ahrefs-Class)

This document outlines how to build an SEO analyzer that can evaluate a submitted URL and generate actionable feedback comparable to tools like SEMrush and Ahrefs.

## 1) Product Goal

Build a platform where a user enters any URL and receives:
- **Technical SEO diagnostics** (crawlability, indexability, performance, schema, internal linking)
- **On-page SEO scoring** (content quality, metadata, headings, keyword usage)
- **Backlink intelligence** (link profile quality, anchor text, toxicity signals)
- **Keyword and SERP intelligence** (rank tracking, keyword gap, intent mapping)
- **Competitive benchmarking** (against selected competitors)
- **Prioritized recommendations** (what to fix first and why)

## 2) Feature Parity Target (SEMrush/Ahrefs-like)

### A. Site Audit
- Full crawler with configurable depth, robots handling, canonical resolution
- Duplicate title/meta/H1 detection
- Broken links (4xx/5xx), redirect chains/loops
- Orphan page detection
- Mobile-friendliness signals
- Core Web Vitals (lab + field where available)
- Schema validation coverage
- XML sitemap and robots.txt validation

### B. On-Page Analyzer
- URL-level SEO score (0-100)
- Intent-content match
- Topic coverage and semantic gap
- Readability + entity coverage
- Internal/external link quality checks
- Image alt coverage and media optimization

### C. Keyword Intelligence
- Keyword discovery by topic/domain
- Difficulty, volume, trend, CPC estimations
- SERP feature tracking (snippets, PAA, local pack, video)
- Position tracking by location/device

### D. Backlink Intelligence
- Referring domains/pages growth
- Anchor distribution and mismatch flags
- Lost/new backlinks timelines
- Link toxicity risk scoring
- Competitor link gap

### E. Competitor & Gap Analysis
- Domain overlap analysis
- Keyword gap (missing/weak/shared)
- Content gap (topics competitors rank for but target doesn’t)
- Backlink gap and outreach prospects

### F. Reporting & Feedback UX
- Executive summary + technical drill-down
- Severity labels: **Critical / High / Medium / Low**
- Impact estimate: traffic upside and confidence
- Fix recipes with examples
- Re-crawl and trend tracking

## 3) URL-First User Flow

When user submits a URL:
1. Normalize URL and detect canonical host/protocol.
2. Check robots/sitemap and crawl allowance.
3. Launch async crawl + render pass (HTML and JS-rendered states).
4. Extract page/content/link/metadata/signals.
5. Run rules engine + ML scoring pipelines.
6. Generate:
   - Page-level issues
   - Site-level issues
   - Prioritized fix queue
7. Return dashboard + downloadable report.
8. Schedule periodic monitoring if enabled.

## 4) System Architecture

### Ingestion Layer
- URL validator + queue producer
- Message queue (Kafka/SQS/RabbitMQ)
- Crawl scheduler with politeness and rate controls

### Crawl/Render Layer
- Fast HTTP crawler for static analysis
- Headless rendering cluster for JS-heavy pages
- Retry and anti-loop protections

### Data Processing Layer
- HTML parser + DOM extractor
- Link graph builder
- Content NLP pipeline (entities, topics, intent)
- Performance pipeline (LCP/CLS/INP proxies + Lighthouse jobs)

### Intelligence Layer
- Rule-based SEO checks
- Scoring engine (technical, content, authority)
- Recommendation engine with severity and expected impact
- Competitor comparison service

### Storage Layer
- Relational DB for entities and tasks
- Columnar/warehouse for analytics
- Search index for fast issue lookup
- Object storage for crawl snapshots/reports

### API & App Layer
- REST/GraphQL API
- Dashboard (overview, issues, trends, competitor modules)
- Alerts (email/webhook/slack)

## 5) Data Model (Core Entities)

- `Project` (domain, locale, device profile)
- `CrawlJob` (status, depth, started_at, finished_at)
- `Page` (url, canonical, status_code, indexability)
- `Issue` (type, severity, confidence, detected_at)
- `Keyword` (query, volume, kd, intent)
- `Ranking` (keyword_id, url, position, date, location, device)
- `Backlink` (source_url, target_url, anchor, quality_score)
- `Competitor` (domain, overlap metrics)

## 6) Scoring Framework

Weighted score (example):
- Technical SEO: 35%
- Content relevance/quality: 30%
- Authority/backlinks: 25%
- UX/performance: 10%

Issue priority score:
`Priority = Severity x Impact x Confidence x EffortInverse`

This enables “fix this first” recommendations rather than only listing errors.

## 7) Feedback Quality (SEMrush/Ahrefs Style)

Each recommendation should include:
- **What is wrong**
- **Why it matters** (ranking/CTR/indexability impact)
- **How to fix** (step-by-step)
- **Example implementation**
- **Expected outcome**
- **Re-check status** after fix deployment

## 8) Build Plan

### Phase 1 (MVP: 6-10 weeks)
- URL submission + crawl + technical checks
- On-page analyzer for single URL and small sites
- Basic report and issue prioritization

### Phase 2
- Keyword tracking + competitor modules
- Backlink ingestion and scoring
- Scheduled audits and alerts

### Phase 3
- AI-assisted recommendations and rewrite suggestions
- Traffic impact forecasting
- Agency-grade white-label reporting

## 9) Quality & Trust Requirements

- Transparent scoring formulas
- Deterministic rule checks with evidence links
- Reproducible crawl snapshots
- Differential runs (before/after fixes)
- SLA and robust error handling for large sites

## 10) Suggested Tech Stack

- **Backend:** Node.js/TypeScript or Python (FastAPI)
- **Crawl:** custom crawler + Playwright/Chromium workers
- **Queue:** Kafka or SQS
- **DB:** PostgreSQL + ClickHouse/BigQuery
- **Search index:** OpenSearch/Elasticsearch
- **Frontend:** Next.js + charts
- **Infra:** Kubernetes + autoscaling workers

## 11) Success Metrics

- Crawl success rate
- Issue detection precision/recall (golden QA sets)
- Mean time to first report
- Recommendation adoption rate
- Ranking/traffic improvement after fixes

## 12) Reality Check

Matching SEMrush/Ahrefs at full depth is a **large multi-year effort** due to:
- Massive backlink index requirements
- Global SERP data collection complexity
- Ongoing algorithm and feature maintenance

A focused product can still be highly competitive by specializing in:
- faster technical auditing,
- clearer actionable feedback,
- and better workflow automation.
